fact WorkItem(id: "WI-568", description: some(value: "Add cut (!) as a kernel control primitive in the SLD resolver. Implements proposal 033 §Future work (Cut and the barrier mechanism); promote that section to a child proposal 033.1. Cut commits to the current rule invocation: given a(?x) :- b(?x), !, c(?x), when ! fires it discards (i) other clauses of a still queued at the parent ChoicePoint and (ii) every ChoicePoint created during resolution of b(?x) (push_choice Continuations and nested rule unfoldings); choice points created AFTER ! (during c) are untouched. DESIGN (proposal 033 lines 207-222): (1) per-invocation BarrierId allocated in with_fresh_vars alongside the fresh Globals -- BarrierId is to cut what VarId is to a query variable: a fresh, monotonic, per-invocation tag. (2) ChoicePoint gains barrier_at_creation: BarrierId, tagged when each choice point is pushed (push_choice, multi-alt rule unfold, occurrence backtracking). (3) cut(?barrier) builtin: the ! body syntax opens to cut(B) where B is the enclosing rule barrier (parallels DeBruijn-var opening); semantics = walk the candidate / choice-point stack and remove every alternative (Rule, Occurrence, Continuation, Assumption alike) whose barrier_at_creation is B or descended from B. (4) Disjunction-cut interaction falls out for free = Prolog transparent-to-outer-cut, opaque-to-inner-cut: a cut in a body that contains or(...) prunes the push_choice Continuations of that or (tagged with the outer barrier transitively); a cut inside the body of or itself (or any inner rule) prunes only within its own barrier. SCOPE CORRECTION (load-bearing): proposal 033 Requirement 3 claims cut is expressible as rewrites without core changes -- over-optimistic and contradicted by its own §Future work. push_choice CREATES choice points; cut PRUNES them back to a barrier (the inverse), which genuinely requires the two CORE resolver additions above (BarrierId allocator in with_fresh_vars + barrier_at_creation on ChoicePoint). The no-core-changes claim holds only for the DERIVED combinators. FILES: kb/resolve.rs (ChoicePoint field, candidate-stack prune, step handling of cut alongside Not / HoApply / PushChoice), kb/mod.rs (with_fresh_vars BarrierId alloc, BuiltinTag::Cut, register anthill.kernel.cut), grammar (tree-sitter + fastparse: parse ! as a body goal) + parse IR, kernel.anthill (operation cut). DERIVED FOLLOW-ONS (separate WIs, each a pure rewrite over cut, no further core): once(g) = (g, !) lifted into a synthesized rule; if-then-else(c, t, e) = (c, !, t) ; e; findall = meta-call plus collection. SUBSTRATE ALREADY DELIVERED: push_choice (WI-075, Verified) supplies the ChoicePoint / Continuation machinery that cut prunes. TESTS: commit-to-first-clause (a(?x):-b,!,c discards later a-clauses); inner choice-point pruning (! after a branching b drops the alternatives of b); disjunction transparency (outer cut prunes inner or; inner cut opaque to outer or); cut + NAF (cut within a not(...) scope); cut + delay / residualization (a barrier whose owning frame floundered). IMMEDIATE CONSUMER (NON-BLOCKING): WI-089 anthill.realization.calculate_type_mapping uses a NAF existence-wrapper for the specific-key-wins-else-default priority; once cut lands it simplifies to the clean TypeMapping(...)!, default form. WI-089 does NOT depend on this. scaland parity (grammar + loader; resolver port if scaland resolves) tracked as a follow-up."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-075"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-26T07:25:06Z"))
